{
  "opportunity_id": "proc_9357b62546",
  "source": "content_cluster",
  "title": "Monthly plant gas nomination emails for Morgan's Point MTBE, re-keyed by hand",
  "task_class": "gas_nomination",
  "label_mechanical": "Gas nomination and scheduling: submit monthly / gas / nomination",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "Each month a counterparty contact (EGPFC) emails the logistics desk a nomination stating the natural gas requirements for the MTBE Plant at Morgan's Point for the coming month, using near-identical wording every time (\"EGPFC nominates the following natural gas requirements ... for October 2000\"). The logistics recipient takes the stated volumes and sets up or updates the corresponding deal and delivery setup so the gas is scheduled. Related plants and setups appear in the same stream \u2014 a Katy Plant first-of-month nomination and a \"setup for Josey\" \u2014 and some months arrive as revisions rather than fresh submissions. The exchange ends when the setup matches the nominated volumes; in one case it ends permanently (\"This is the last month we will be buying this gas!!!!\").",
    "where_it_stalls": "The nomination arrives as prose and numbers in an email body, so the volumes must be re-entered by the recipient, and a meaningful share of the messages are corrections rather than first submissions: volumes are changed after the fact (\"I went ahead and changed the volume down to 12,400 from 13,000\"), mid-month effective dates force a re-issued setup (\"Here's REVISED February 2000 (effective 2/17/00)\"), and at least one change was agreed verbally and then dropped (\"this change was missed but was discussed with you last week\"). Setup also blocks on inputs held by another group \u2014 one sender is still waiting on a transport number from a named person in the recipient's shop.",
    "why_it_recurs": "The nomination is monthly and per-plant, so a new email is required every month for each plant, and any mid-month volume change requires a second, revised email against the same month.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A fixed submission form or template that captures plant, meter, effective date and daily volume as fields, feeding the deal setup directly instead of a prose email that is re-keyed; pair it with a confirmation reply back to the nominator showing the volumes as entered, so verbally agreed changes cannot be missed and revisions supersede rather than duplicate.",
    "coherence": "tight"
  },
